<p>President Trump said the United States could keep its naval blockade of Iranian ports in place for months after rejecting an Iranian proposal to reopen the Strait of Hormuz and lift the blockade before broader nuclear talks continued. A White House official said Trump discussed with oil executives how to sustain pressure while cushioning U.S. consumers from the energy-market fallout. Brent crude surged above $125 a barrel in Asian trading on Thursday, its highest level since 2022, as traders priced in a prolonged disruption to Middle East energy shipments. Diplomacy remained stalled after false starts. Back-channel mediation continued as Washington and Tehran traded public threats over shipping restrictions and nuclear demands.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/XnmCJGmWPsqeJNy6KnzVZsOGrV9MysyxRddxE_aC4y-9RB3th89BeZ1q2y5rGzdpCcpmYWOoZy8T-fm6SDnRVxuStF9Us7_tJHygYqE4NBbW' alt='US and Iran flags are seen in this illustration created on June 18, 2025.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Political cost: Reports said the extended conflict had hurt Trump’s poll numbers and weakened Republicans’ midterm prospects, while Le Monde noted pressure from allies and from parts of his base.</li><li>Military options: Axios reported that U.S. Central Command prepared a plan for “short and powerful” strikes on Iran, and Trump was due to receive a briefing on potential strikes on Thursday.</li><li>Shipping disruption: U.S. forces blocked 42 vessels traveling to or from Iranian ports during the blockade, according to a Spanish report citing U.S. military information.</li></ul><blockquote>The blockade is somewhat more effective than the bombing. - President Donald Trump</blockquote><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>White House: A White House official framed the Tuesday meeting as part of Trump’s regular outreach to energy executives for feedback on domestic and international energy markets, listing domestic production, Venezuela, oil futures, natural gas and shipping among the topics. (<a href='https://www.brecorder.com/news/40418875/trump-eyeing-iran-blockade-lasting-months-if-needed-white-house-official'>Business Recorder</a>)</li><li>Pakistan: A Pakistani source told Reuters that Islamabad was trying to prevent escalation while Washington and Tehran continued exchanging messages on a possible deal. (<a href='https://tribune.com.pk/story/2605603/trump-holds-talks-on-prolonged-iran-blockade'>The Express Tribune</a>)</li><li>Oil traders: Traders interpreted the White House meeting as a signal that U.S. pressure on Iran and restrictions around the Strait of Hormuz could last longer. (<a href='https://tocka.com.mk/vesti/554630/cenite-na-naftata-skoknaa-nad-120-dolari-brent-na-najvisoko-nivo-od-2022-godina'>Tocka</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/apr/30/oil-price-news-highest-since-2022-us-iran-ceasefire-strait-of-hormuz'>Oil price tops $120 a barrel after Trump warns Iran blockade could last ‘months’</a> - theguardian.com</li><li><a href='https://www.scmp.com/news/world/middle-east/article/3351904/trump-says-us-blockade-could-last-months-warns-iran-get-smart-soon'>Trump warns US naval blockade against Iran could last months, sending oil soaring</a> - scmp.com</li><li><a href='https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/4/30/oil-prices-soar-on-fears-of-long-supply-disruption-us-siege-of-iran-ports'>Oil prices soar on fears of long supply disruption, US siege of Iran ports</a> - aljazeera.com</li><li><a href='https://www.semafor.com/article/04/29/2026/oil-rises-as-trump-rejects-irans-peace-proposal'>Oil rises as Trump rejects Iran&#x27;s peace proposal</a> - semafor.com</li><li><a href='https://www.dawn.com/news/1996253/us-turns-down-iranian-proposal-to-end-war'>US turns down Iranian proposal to end war</a> - dawn.com</li><li><a href='https://www.lemonde.fr/en/international/article/2026/04/30/trump-warns-iran-blockade-could-last-months-sending-oil-soaring_6752996_4.html'>Trump warns Iran blockade could l